          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Root user + docker.sock mounted: one app bug = **full host compromise**",
            "No memory limit: container eats host RAM, kernel may kill something else",
            "`ENV API_KEY=...` in Dockerfile: leaked to anyone who pulls the image",
            "Default json-file logs unbounded: disk fills, host falls over",
            "`FROM node:latest`: surprise upgrades, no reproducible security state"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Signals and readiness",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --name c -p 8080:80 img",
            "docker ps -a            # all states",
            "docker stop c; docker start c",
            "docker rm -f c; docker logs -f c",
            "docker exec -it c sh",
            "docker inspect c; docker stats"
          ],
          "note": "rm -f kills then removes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ENTRYPOINT [\"python\",\"app.py\"]",
            "HEALTHCHECK --interval=10s \\",
            "  CMD curl -f localhost/hz",
            "# run: docker run --init img"
          ],
          "note": "shell form: sh is PID 1, eats SIGTERM"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker stop` sends ==SIGTERM==; app must catch it and finish in-flight work",
            "**Exec-form** ENTRYPOINT makes the app PID 1 so the signal reaches it",
            "`--init` (tini) reaps zombies and forwards signals when the app cannot",
            "==HEALTHCHECK== turns 'started' into 'ready'; `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` waits for it"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mounting `/var/run/docker.sock`: that container **owns** the host",
            "Running as root **and** mounting the socket: one app bug = full compromise",
            "No memory cap: the kernel ==OOM killer== may kill something else",
            "Default `json-file` logs grow unbounded until the disk is full"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
