        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition: layers move once",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An image is a stack of ==layers==, each named by a `sha256` digest",
            "`docker pull` downloads **only** the layers not already on the host",
            "`docker push` uploads **only** the layers the registry is missing",
            "Same digest = same bytes, so a copy is never sent twice",
            "Layers are shared across images: one `node:22-slim` base, many apps"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Reading a pull",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Only Missing Layers Move"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reading Pull and Push Output: Digest Dedupe",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker pull nginx:1.27",
            "3f2a...: Already exists",
            "9c1b...: Pull complete",
            "a77d...: Pull complete",
            "Status: Downloaded newer image"
          ],
          "note": "Already exists = zero bytes over network"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Layer",
            "On host?",
            "Network"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "base os",
              "yes",
              "==skipped=="
            ],
            [
              "apt deps",
              "yes",
              "skipped"
            ],
            [
              "app code",
              "no",
              "**downloaded**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why the second pull is instant",
          "text": "Nothing was cached by the tag. The layers were already on disk under the same ==digest==, so Docker printed `Already exists` and moved zero bytes."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Reading a push",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker push reg/app:1.5",
            "3f2a...: Layer already exists",
            "b410...: Pushed",
            "1.5: digest: sha256:8e1f..."
          ],
          "note": "registry dedupes by digest, not by tag"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Registry asks for each digest first; ==only new blobs== are uploaded",
            "A one-line code change ships the top layer, not the whole base",
            "`docker history img` shows which layers a change actually rebuilt",
            "Manifest lists digests; it is tiny and always transferred"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
