        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Design for small transfers",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Share one pinned base across services: pulled once per host",
            "Put ==volatile files last== so only the top layer changes",
            "Fat single-layer images resend everything on every deploy",
            "Deploy nodes pull faster when the base is already cached"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`COPY . .` **before** installing deps: every push resends deps",
            "A different base per service: no layer sharing, slow pulls",
            "Squashing all layers: one byte changed, whole image re-uploaded",
            "Assuming a fast push means a small image; it was just cached",
            "`docker system prune -a` on builders: next pull downloads everything"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
